## What this predicate means

**A `bypasses` B** — actor (or actor+context tuple) memorial A is EXEMPT from rule memorial B.  The exception/override declaration in the substrate's rules-as-first-class architecture.  Modeled on GitHub Rulesets' `bypass_actors` mechanism per the rules-as-first-class ADR + cornerstone modern-tooling broad-survey.  Lets specific actors operate outside a rule's enforcement when authorized exemption exists.

## Substrate identity

