## Formal signature

`{{predicate-name}} : {{domain}} × {{range}} → Bool`

## Characteristics

- **Asymmetric** — actor bypasses rule doesn't imply rule bypasses actor (OWL 2 RL `prp-asyp`)
- **Irreflexive** — no actor bypasses themselves; no rule bypasses itself (OWL 2 RL `prp-irp`)
- **NOT transitive** — exemption doesn't chain through actor delegation

## When to use bypasses

Use `bypasses` on actor memorials (or actor+context tuple memorials) when:

- An actor has authorized exemption from a rule in some context
- A meta-actor (e.g., the project admin) needs override capability
- A test-mode actor needs to skip production rules

The substrate's rule-engine layer queries `bypasses` at rule-firing time — if the firing actor (in the firing context) bypasses the rule, the rule's enforcement is short-circuited.

